    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen enabling coverage analysis in a package compiled with the shared utility module, coverage.py complains that it cannot find the module source:\n```\n  File \"/opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.12.13/x64/lib/python3.12/site-packages/coverage/python.py\", line 67, in get_python_source\n    raise NoSource(f\"No source for code: '{filename}'.\", slug=\"no-source\")\ncoverage.exceptions.NoSource: No source for code: '/home/runner/work/cython/cython/Cython/_shared.pyx'.\n```\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nIn general, it is unlikely that users care about the shared utility module when it comes to coverage analysis.\n\nPossible ideas:\n- The shared module could be ignored in general, but it might be difficult to detect.\n- All modules for which the source code cannot be found could be marked as excluded, but that might also impact user modules.\n- Require users to exclude the module themselves in their coverage config.\n\n### OS\n\n_No response_\n\n### Python version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Cython version\n\nmaster\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
